        "seed-1": {
          "type": "seed",
          "settings": {
            "label": "Roast chicken, Friday night",
            "answer": "Roast chicken wants grip and a little sweetness to meet the skin.\n\nNON3 — toasted cinnamon, yuzu and orange pith, with enough grip to hold the fat. Serve it cold in a wine glass, not a tumbler.\n\nIf the bird comes with something green and bitter, pour NON1 alongside.",
            "picks": "NON3,NON1",
            "short_label": "Roast chicken, Friday night",
            "intent": "dinner",
            "show_on_mobile": true
          }
        },
        "seed-2": {
          "type": "seed",
          "settings": {
            "label": "Is this just grape juice?",
            "answer": "No. Nothing here is fermented and nothing is de-alcoholised.\n\nEach bottle is cooked — ingredients toasted, reduced, salted, acidified — then blended for the structure alcohol used to provide. Tannin from tea and skins, salinity from kombu or salt, acid from citrus and vinegar.\n\nIt reads dry, not sweet. That surprises people.",
            "picks": "NON2,NON3"
          }
        },
        "seed-3": {
          "type": "seed",
          "settings": {
            "label": "A night off, not a compromise",
            "answer": "Then keep the ritual: cold bottle, real glass, something worth discussing.\n\nStart with the Everyday Set — rosé, white, red, three seats at the table. Nothing here is a smaller version of a drink. It is built from zero, cooked rather than de-alcoholised, and it holds its own next to the food.",
            "picks": "SET,NON1",
            "short_label": "A night off, not a compromise",
            "intent": "night_off",
            "show_on_mobile": true
          }
        },
        "seed-4": {
          "type": "seed",
          "settings": {
            "label": "Gift for a chef",
            "answer": "Chefs taste for structure, so lead with NON2 — caramelised pear and kombu, savoury enough to be interesting on its own.\n\nPut it in the Stopper Set so nothing is wasted between services. Seven days of carbonation, kept cold.",
            "picks": "NON2,SET",
            "short_label": "Gift for a chef",
            "intent": "gift",
            "show_on_mobile": true
          }
        },
